A vintage-style illustration depicting two 10-year-old twin boys hunched over a wooden workbench covered with scattered electronic components, circuit boards, tiny gears, and a soldering iron emitting a thin wisp of smoke. Their faces glow with intense curiosity and concentration as they examine the mysterious innards of a partially assembled wheeled robot kit. An elderly man with weathered hands stands behind them, guiding one boy's grip on the soldering iron. Warm amber lamplight illuminates the scene from above, casting long shadows across blueprints and instruction manuals spread beneath the components. The color palette features sepia tones with pops of copper, brass, and deep forest green from the circuit boards. Small screws and resistors are scattered like treasure across the worn wood surface. The atmosphere captures that magical moment of discovery when a pile of parts transforms into possibility.
